    "### 13b-FIX. Validation Split for Checkpoint Selection (Journal Fix)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Issue resolved**: The original DistilBERT training used `eval_dataset=test_dataset_bert`\n",
    "with `load_best_model_at_end=True`.  This caused the test set to influence\n",
    "checkpoint selection (indirect test-set leakage), making reported metrics\n",
    "non-valid held-out results.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Fix applied**: The training set is now split 90/10 (train/validation).\n",
    "The validation set is used for `eval_dataset` during training (checkpoint\n",
    "selection via `load_best_model_at_end=True`).  The original 20% test set\n",
    "is kept completely untouched and evaluated **once** after training completes.\n",
    "\n",
    "This follows the standard `TRAIN → VALIDATION → (freeze) → TEST` protocol\n",
    "required for journal publication.\n"
